skill: "co-marketing-term-sheet-builder"
sections[3]:
  - "# co-marketing-term-sheet-builder\n\nDraft the commercial skeleton of a co-marketing or joint-venture arrangement before legal drafting starts: rights, spend splits, fund usage rules, lead ownership and exit terms. Use once a target agrees to explore a partnership and always before any draft agreement is written or shared externally.\n\nOwner: role-partnership-bd-manager (pod-growth, marketing). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - search_web\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"partner-map.toon target entry; deal parameters from the operator; standing policy liability-cap-policy.toon; related existing agreements via legal-contract-truth-engine\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/growth/term-sheet.toon with parties, scope, rights, spend_split, lead_ownership, term, termination; handoff to role-contract-manager\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Capture the deal parameters in one place: scope, duration, marketing spend split, fund governance and lead ownership; missing parameters are ask_question items, never assumptions.\n2. Check the partner register and pull any existing agreements with the same counterparty through legal-contract-truth-engine so the term sheet does not contradict a signed clause.\n3. Draft the term sheet clause skeleton: grant of rights, brand usage rules, spend split with currency and caps, fund usage evidence requirements, lead ownership and non-solicit window.\n4. Apply liability-cap-policy.toon: insert the standard cap and mark any deviation as a red-flag for legal review rather than negotiating it here.\n5. State termination triggers explicitly (underperformance threshold, breach, change of control) with notice periods in days.\n6. Mark every open commercial point as OPEN with the decision owner; a term sheet with silent gaps becomes a contract dispute later.\n7. Emit ask_question to the operator for every OPEN point above the spend threshold that needs a human call.\n8. Hand term-sheet.toon to role-contract-manager for redlining and formal drafting; stop there - this role does not negotiate final legal language.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nterm sheet to role-contract-manager; executed terms logged back to partner-register.toon.\n"
